  "notes": [
    "Every attempt ended by delivering a completion report through the hand-back; none said it could not complete, and no transcript ends abnormally. Wall times are all below the 35-minute budget (the longest is 1139 s).",
    "The audit script flagged 9 attempts: 5 for hits in tool inputs only, 1 for an exposure in a tool output only and 3 for both. Each flagged access was read in its transcript. 8 pass: their flags are false positives, files of their own in /tmp (the container's temporary directory), harness notices naming files they never opened, or a call that was denied before it ran. CS-02-fresh-A-final-1 is confirmed: it wrote three helper files of its own into the build session's scratch directory, read them back and ran them there, then deleted them. It read files outside its workspace, so it is excluded from every analysis; it is registered with audit.passed false.",
    "The sensitivity analysis of protocol §18.1 excludes all 9 flagged attempts, which leaves 11.",
    "Of the passing attempts, three (CS-02-fresh-B-u1-5, CS-02-fresh-B-final-1, CS-02-fresh-B-final-2) wrote files of their own in /tmp, which §18.1 counts as a system location, and one (CS-02-fresh-B-u1-3) made one call that also named a file outside its workspace, which the permission classifier denied before it ran (see audit_report).",
    "Harness context outside tool inputs and outputs (reminders listing the build session's task titles, and the session's working directory and scratch path) reached all 20 attempts; it holds no task material (see audit_report). The scratch path it names is where CS-02-fresh-A-final-1 wrote its helper files.",
    "The patch policy removed the attempts' edits of test files from every captured patch (tests/test_storages.py in 19, tests/test_middlewares.py in 2, a new test file in 1); the attempts' workspaces are unchanged."
  ],
